docs/findings/649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md:631:The growth is a little less than linear: the second stream costs 4,739 LUTs and the third and fourth 3,464 each.
docs/findings/649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md:636:At 60,454 LUTs it lies 10,328 below the line's value at eight streams; the blocks it prunes (the render lane, the latency taps, the loopback lane and the probes) are about 1,200 routed LUTs of that, so the growth per stream falls further above four streams.
docs/findings/649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md:681:Yosys's per-stream LUT figure is about 3.6 times Vivado's, and its residuals (negative at one and four streams, positive at two) show the growth is sub-linear: a large first step, then a falling cost per stream, as in the Vivado anchors.
docs/findings/649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md:797:- **Stream contexts** dominate. One more stream each way, with its stream ports, adds 5,886 Yosys LUTs and 1,367 FFs on the linear fit, and the residuals (RMS 1,989; negative at 1 and 8 stream ports, positive at 2 and 4) show the growth is sub-linear: the first added stream costs 10,780 LUTs, and the next ones 5,632 and then 5,229 each. Most of it is the ACMP talker, which Yosys maps at many times Vivado's size: the portability finding of the [#234 reconciliation](234_PP_SHADOW_AREA_BASELINE.md#yosys-reconciliation). The [Vivado anchors](#streams-and-channels) measure the real per-stream cost.
docs/findings/README.md:25:| [649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md](649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md) | Side project of the #229 area epic and input to #640 (#649): the shipping 1x1 route at dev `241f9184` mapped to every one of its 175 blocks, each block's LUT, FF, RAMB and DSP figures read from both the utilization report and the placed-cell census, its CARRY4 and slices from the census, and the totals tied to the `route-1x1` record, and the resource cost of every design parameter: 59 Yosys sweep points (52 guard-clean, 7 refused), four Vivado anchors at 1, 2, 4 and 8 streams, the SoC options with the CPU, cache and L2 variants priced out of context from a scratch recipe copy, and the redundancy second port | Current, measurement only. Each stream per direction costs 3,828 LUT out of context, two thirds in the processor, with a falling cost per added stream; channels and the TDM capture width cost nothing; the low-function-cost prunes total up to about 1,200 routed LUT, a tenth of the NFR-RES-01 gap. Yosys does not enforce the RTL's elaboration guards, and the builder accepts an 8x8 TDM8 configuration the saved-state backend refuses (235 names against 128) |
